## 🚀 Setup Instructions

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.9 or higher
- Azure Student Account (free $100 credit)
- Groq API Account (free tier)
- Google Cloud Project with Sheets API enabled

### Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/india-restaurant-finder.git
cd india-restaurant-finder
```

### Step 2: Create Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Activate (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate
```

### Step 3: Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 4: Set Up Azure Cognitive Search

1. Go to https://portal.azure.com
2. Create a Resource Group
3. Create Azure Cognitive Search service (Free tier)
4. Note down the endpoint and admin key

### Step 5: Get Groq API Key

1. Visit https://console.groq.com
2. Sign up/login
3. Create API key

### Step 6: Set Up Google Sheets

1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com
2. Enable Google Sheets API
3. Create Service Account
4. Download credentials JSON
5. Share your Google Sheet with the service account email

### Step 7: Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```env
AZURE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://your-service.search.windows.net
AZURE_SEARCH_KEY=your_azure_admin_key
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=your_google_sheet_id
GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_PATH=credentials.json
```

### Step 8: Create Azure Search Index

```bash
python setup_azure_index.py
```

### Step 9: Test RAG Engine

```bash
python rag_engine.py
```

### Step 10: Run the Application

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

The application will open in your browser at `http://localhost:8501`

